<p>Testing electrical and mechanical items is performed by qualified technicians who follow safety protocols, including the use of insulated gloves and grounding equipment. Any malfunctioning units are isolated, labeled, and reported for replacement or repair, preventing downstream issues.</p>

<p>Furniture placement emphasizes a clean aesthetic and functional layout. Teams use soft‑tipped rollers and protective pads to avoid scratches, and they verify that all items are free of dents, scratches, or missing components before final positioning.</p>

<p>Debris removal is executed swiftly to maintain a tidy workspace and comply with Packer’s sustainability standards. Cardboard is flattened for recycling, while foam and plastics are sorted for appropriate disposal. The area is inspected one final time to ensure no remnants remain, guaranteeing a pristine environment ready for immediate use.</p></div>
